WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.499
Welcome to Grade 4 English, Unit 6: People in Society.

2
00:00:03.579 --> 00:00:10.193
Unit 6 is about the people who keep a community
working: the helpers, the leaders, and the newcomers.

3
00:00:10.273 --> 00:00:18.080
You will meet a caretaker, a carpenter, an engineer and a
merchant, then governors, senators, lawyers and the military,

4
00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:24.178
and finally artists, photographers, messengers,
refugees, immigrants, tenants and consumers.

5
00:00:24.258 --> 00:00:31.203
You will use the Present Simple to say what each person
does, should and mustn't to give advice and rules,

6
00:00:31.283 --> 00:00:36.572
prepositions to say where people go, and
the past tenses to retell what happened.

7
00:00:36.652 --> 00:00:44.061
By the end you will describe the helpers in your own town,
just as Amal does in the story “The Community Parade”.

8
00:00:44.141 --> 00:00:49.629
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

9
00:00:49.709 --> 00:00:51.411
By the end of this unit,

10
00:00:51.491 --> 00:00:58.613
you will be able to name and describe at least
twenty jobs and roles that people play in society.

11
00:00:58.693 --> 00:01:04.999
You will also explain what different workers
and leaders do, using the Present Simple.

12
00:01:05.079 --> 00:01:09.974
You will also give advice and state
rules using should and mustn't.

13
00:01:10.054 --> 00:01:12.721
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

14
00:01:12.801 --> 00:01:18.895
Your vocabulary work begins with these words: caretaker,
carpenter, labourer, engineer, merchant, governor.

15
00:01:18.975 --> 00:01:23.569
Listen to each pronunciation in the
vocabulary lab, study its meaning in context,

16
00:01:23.649 --> 00:01:27.203
and use the word accurately in
your own discussion and writing.

17
00:01:27.283 --> 00:01:33.201
The reading sequence includes The People of Our
Town and Two Neighbours: A Refugee and an Immigrant.

18
00:01:33.281 --> 00:01:34.040
Read actively.

19
00:01:34.120 --> 00:01:38.179
Identify each text's central ideas,
notice viewpoint and reliability,

20
00:01:38.259 --> 00:01:42.077
and support every inference with
relevant evidence from the text.

21
00:01:42.157 --> 00:01:46.276
The first language focus is Present
Simple: describing everyday jobs.

22
00:01:46.356 --> 00:01:51.510
We use the Present Simple for routines,
facts, and things that happen again and again.

23
00:01:51.590 --> 00:01:58.144
It suits jobs perfectly, because most jobs repeat every
day: “The caretaker cleans the school every morning.”

24
00:01:58.224 --> 00:02:04.778
Notice the structure in the model examples, then apply
it deliberately in connected sentences and paragraphs.

25
00:02:04.858 --> 00:02:08.446
In speaking, you will complete Speaking 1: Describe a Job.

26
00:02:08.526 --> 00:02:12.683
Organise your ideas, use evidence
and respond clearly to questions.

27
00:02:12.763 --> 00:02:15.909
In writing, you will plan, draft, check and revise.

28
00:02:15.989 --> 00:02:19.260
Use the success criteria before submitting your work.

29
00:02:19.340 --> 00:02:20.798
You are ready to begin.

30
00:02:20.878 --> 00:02:27.417
Start with the vocabulary lab, continue through
reading and comprehension, apply the grammar focus,

31
00:02:27.497 --> 00:02:30.627
and complete the speaking and writing practices.

32
00:02:30.707 --> 00:02:38.048
Use AI English for hints and feedback any time, and bring
your questions to a live session too if you join one.
